Subject: [PATCH 11/24] Test a new process where only the data file cannot sync
 against decision 8

The restart test is split: where neither file syncs, a durable commit is
refused before it writes a frame (decision 3) and the failure is sticky
(decision 6); where only the data file cannot sync, the new process's
commits are expected durable in the kept WAL, the header anchored there
(decisions 8 and 10), and to survive a power loss. The second fails until
the header frame is implemented. The header-rule message constant goes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
